# No unnecessary type casting

Do not use `as` (or other casts) to silence the type checker. Prefer accurate types so property access is legal without assertions.

Cast only when there is no sound alternative (e.g. a true boundary with unknown runtime shape that cannot be modeled).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — cast at every use site
readonly #inner: globalThis.Request;

get duplex() {
  return (this.#inner as Request & { duplex?: "half" }).duplex;
}

// ✅ GOOD — widen the stored type once; callers need no cast
type NativeRequest = globalThis.Request & {
  duplex?: "half";
};

readonly #inner: NativeRequest;

get duplex() {
  return this.#inner.duplex;
}
```

Do not cast through `any` or double-assert. Prefer narrowing (`instanceof`, typeof checks, generics) over `as`.
